The TypeScript adaptation computes the float paths with one Math.fround per C
operation and the double paths in IEEE double, runs channels sequentially
(slice threading does not change the result), allocates one owned output frame
per input frame instead of filtering in place, and refuses option expressions,
quoted values, timeline enable and runtime commands instead of evaluating them.
It adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The original source and full notices remain in
the pinned upstream submodule.
